    <p><br></p>
    <h2 id=3D"DWHappaccesscontrolviaCompasscurrent,future,transitional-Acce=
ssControlEnforcement">Access Control Enforcement</h2>
    <p>Source: <a href=3D"https://wiki.bnc.ca/spaces/NDSKW/pages/1472506895=
/Okta+Integration+with+NBIN+Landing+page" rel=3D"nofollow">Okta Integration=
 with NBIN Landing page - NBIN Data Services team - Confluence</a></p>
    <br>
    <ul>
     <li data-uuid=3D"ef044d20-703e-45ab-b456-a58c755039c4">According to th=
e solution, two calls will be made to FUM API for access control enforcemen=
t:</li>
    </ul>
    <ol>
     <li data-uuid=3D"0dd61709-d28d-4608-bf54-a2002e0acfb9">List of resourc=
es: /iam/access-control/resources/dwh_ui_module/assignments/users/me</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"4c48284c-1c98-4ca6-afa5-9b53a17fa1e9">List of permiss=
ions: /iam/access-control/capabilities/dwh-{capability}/scopes/me</li>
    </ol>
    <p>&nbsp;Reference: <a href=3D"https://wiki.bnc.ca/spaces/NDSKW/pages/2=
236572519/OktaScopes-Groups" rel=3D"nofollow">OktaScopes-Groups - NBIN Data=
 Services team - Confluence</a></p>
    <p><br></p>
    <p>:warning:<span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;"> In Compass db, a us=
er account is being assigned to ONE user group only regardless how many AD =
groups the user is assigned to. Further analysis discovers that the capabil=
ity call (second call) would not validate user-to-UG assignment but return =
all scopes for all groups found in the Token.</span></p>
    <p><br></p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <h1 id=3D"DWHappaccesscontrolviaCompasscurrent,future,transitional-Targ=
etState:Decoupling">Target State: Decoupling</h1>
    <p><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;color:#172b4d;">Purpose: Remove=
 the dependency on FUM for web application authentication and authorization=
.</span></p>
    <p><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">Objective: The recommended approach i=
s to leverage IIQ for identity governance and Microsoft Entra ID for authen=
tication and access control. This will simplify the architecture, reduce co=
upling, and align web applications with enterprise IAM standards.</span></p=
>
    <p><br></p>
    <p>JIRA reference: <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://jira.bnc.=
ca/browse/NDS-15905" rel=3D"nofollow">[NDS-15905] Decoupling DWH from FUM -=
 Jira</a></p>
    <p><br></p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <h1 id=3D"DWHappaccesscontrolviaCompasscurrent,future,transitional-Tran=
sitionalState:TemporarySupport">Transitional State: Temporary Support</h1>
    <h2 id=3D"DWHappaccesscontrolviaCompasscurrent,future,transitional-Cont=
ext">Context</h2>
    <ul>
     <li data-uuid=3D"3c33dadc-4fab-49af-ad02-acbfac27ff5f">When Compass la=
unches the <strong>employee access solution</strong>, eligible employees wi=
ll have their Compass access set up in Okta (NBC) tenant and will experienc=
e SSO access to Compass.</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"f05ac897-b62a-4cc9-98af-127627d23935">Currently, ther=
e are primarily three clusters of employees:=20
      <ul>
       <li data-uuid=3D"e8b9ded3-21e7-4ec8-aa78-2b6eda331b1d">Employees who=
 have access to Compass only,</li>
       <li data-uuid=3D"180a08a8-4c3b-4d7f-a1e2-04fd4ac7a217">Employees who=
 have access to both Compass and DWH webapps,</li>
       <li data-uuid=3D"7035bf6e-8025-4308-82d2-ef487394b5b3">Employees who=
 have access to DWH only</li>
      </ul></li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"5484bbc2-590f-4e89-a077-998b5aa88507">
      <p><u>Purpose:</u> <span>Continue to support the access provisioning =
and enforcement of employees with DWH webapp access (blue circle in the dia=
gram) in Compass until the DWH solution is fully decoupled from Compass.</s=
pan></p></li>
    </ul>
    <p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-=
manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" h=
eight=3D"200" src=3D"39e6f15e38c26b282106fe1cf90fd334cd90dbe3a24da443c17911=
def5d01a7b" data-image-src=3D"/download/attachments/2790633185/image-2026-7=
-7_16-6-10.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1783454770386&amp;api=3Dv=
2" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"279063700=
8" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachme=
nt" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image-2026-7-7_16-6-10.png" data-=
base-url=3D"https://wiki.bnc.ca" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image=
/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"2790633185" data-linked-resource=
-container-version=3D"6" tabindex=3D"0" alt=3D"" width=3D"412"></span><span=
 style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">&nbsp;</span></p>
    <p><br></p>
    <h2 id=3D"DWHappaccesscontrolviaCompasscurrent,future,transitional-Conc=
eptualView">Conceptual View</h2>
    <ul>
     <li data-uuid=3D"4495e383-1deb-4823-b98f-7748581bcafe">A new <strong>P=
erson table</strong> will be introduced in Compass, to represent user ident=
ity data only.</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"2ddb0e07-26e6-4221-8094-685004cec962">A person can ha=
ve one or more user access profiles based on the IDP source (NBC vs. NBIN)=
=20
      <ul>
       <li data-uuid=3D"9beab28f-7324-44ec-a405-ee00f6ed1eba"><strong><em>S=
hortId </em></strong>employee account should comprise of Compass access and=
 DWH app access, if both are eligible&nbsp;</li>
       <li data-uuid=3D"32bb8db1-326c-4b23-8a59-2d1176cb9e0a"><strong><em>E=
xternal </em></strong>user account for Compass access only</li>
       <li data-uuid=3D"84844163-e813-4856-af78-30b8de6da8c3">Additional ex=
ternal user accounts, which is rare but possible</li>
      </ul></li>
     <li>See the example below,&nbsp;=20
      <ul>
       <li data-uuid=3D"c4defad4-6d05-4b57-9542-ee5317596d99"><em>SOC007&nb=
sp;</em>is the shortId employee account of user Candi So, and is primarily =
set up for DWH app access only.</li>
       <li data-uuid=3D"237fac9e-359f-4d23-b3a3-8129ede73e8b"><em>candi.so<=
/em> is the primary account of the user's Compass access; the access provis=
ions will be copied to the SOC007 account during the Compass employee acces=
s launch, and the user account will be deleted.</li>
       <li data-uuid=3D"ef1e4632-0f66-482b-9461-49cdd554fb0e"><u>Objective:=
</u></li>
      </ul></li>
    </ul>
    <ol>
     <li data-uuid=3D"43360138-75ed-4a37-9ea9-1e52e92474b6">Transitioned em=
ployees continue to be able to access Compass and DWH webapps as usual.&nbs=
p;</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"24b3f825-087b-4fea-96c3-89c097cffd7b"><span style=3D"=
letter-spacing: 0.0px;">There is a temporary solution to support access pro=
visioning and enforcement of DWH webapp access via Compass until the target=
 state.</span></li>
    </ol>
    <h2 id=3D"DWHappaccesscontrolviaCompasscurrent,future,transitional-"><s=
pan class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-manual-si=
ze"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image confluence-external-resource" d=
raggable=3D"false" width=3D"788" src=3D"https://wiki.bnc.ca/download/attach=
ments/2715081356/image-2026-5-14_15-21-12.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationD=
ate=3D1778786472253&amp;api=3Dv2" data-image-src=3D"https://wiki.bnc.ca/dow=
nload/attachments/2715081356/image-2026-5-14_15-21-12.png?version=3D1&amp;m=
odificationDate=3D1778786472253&amp;api=3Dv2"></span></h2>
    <h2 id=3D"DWHappaccesscontrolviaCompasscurrent,future,transitional-Assu=
mption">Assumption</h2>
    <p>Decision made between Data Solutions product owner and FUM product m=
anager,</p>
    <ul>
     <li data-uuid=3D"b9eb2a02-9af2-4532-a506-7ca1294062dc">After the Compa=
ss employee access launch, an employee must have Compass access if they wan=
t to have Data Solutions webapp access, but not the vice versa.&nbsp;</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-e=
mbedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"=
false" height=3D"161" src=3D"7865d344e29e6d65111c1e55f1784403ffcda0a5985504=
fa7796294113ede6a1" data-image-src=3D"/download/attachments/2790633185/imag=
e-2026-7-7_18-4-38.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1783461878049&amp=
;api=3Dv2" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"2=
790638154" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"=
attachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image-2026-7-7_18-4-38.pn=
g" data-base-url=3D"https://wiki.bnc.ca" data-linked-resource-content-type=
=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"2790633185" data-linked=
-resource-container-version=3D"6" tabindex=3D"0" alt=3D"" width=3D"308"></s=
pan></strong></p>
    <p><br></p>
    <p>:warning: Employees who currently have DWH webapp access only will s=
till be supported in the Transitional state</p>
    <p><br></p>
    <h2 id=3D"DWHappaccesscontrolviaCompasscurrent,future,transitional-Prob=
lemstosolve">Problems to solve</h2>
    <p>After the Compass employee access launch, the user settings of emplo=
yee accounts (<em>shortId</em>) will have been adjusted to comply with the =
new IIQ auto-provisioning flow. There are expected impacts to the schema - =
how user settings are persisted, and the current Manage DWH user manual pro=
cess.</p>
    <p><br></p>
    <div class=3D"table-wrap">
     <table class=3D"relative-table wrapped confluenceTable" style=3D"width=
: 76.76%;">
      <colgroup>
       <col style=3D"width: 8.12476%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 13.3987%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 31.464%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 9.24795%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 37.7646%;">
      </colgroup>
      <tbody>
       <tr>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Category</th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Area</th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Problem / Impact</th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">
         <p>Decision:</p>
         <p>Will Solve / Will Not Solve</p></th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Assessment &amp; Requireme=
nts</th>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <th rowspan=3D"2" scope=3D"rowgroup" class=3D"confluenceTh">Schema<=
/th>
        <th scope=3D"row" class=3D"confluenceTh">DWH user group assignment<=
/th>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"5e1f09cb-a639-4379-be08-d6ab34c42e5b">IIQ will a=
uto-provision Compass user accounts, hence, the UG assignment in Compass ca=
nnot be managed manually</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"b1e87c21-f5db-40af-9db4-28dd4959b75a">In current=
 FUM model, only one UG shall be assigned to a user account. Hence, the DWH=
 UG will not remain.</li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">:tick:<span style=3D"color:#172b4d;"><sp=
an>&nbsp;</span></span></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Tech analysis confirms that the relation between user and DWH U=
G is not essential in access enforcement. Hence, it is safe to detach the D=
WH user-to-UG assignments in Compass.</p>
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"b05fa0ef-11d0-4aca-9698-20d3a1441f05"><span>Duri=
ng the <strong>one-time user load (migration)</strong>, all employee accoun=
ts will be updated with a CX user package/group via IIQ bulk process.</span=
>
           <ul>
            <li data-uuid=3D"8d4010c2-d775-424b-b391-f56d0b21a22c">If an em=
ployee has both DWH and CX access, the DWH UG will be replaced by the CX UG=
 but their DWH resource assignments remain. Expected outcome: Employees wil=
l be able to access both DWH and CX.&nbsp;</li>
            <li data-uuid=3D"a03b83f1-4f22-46e9-bb9f-fb3b7a01dfdf">If an em=
ployee has DWH access only, then their current DWH UG will not be replaced.=
 Expected outcome: No access impact.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>
           </ul></li>
          <li><span>For <strong>new employees</strong>, as stated in the as=
sumption, they must request CX access before&nbsp; DWH access. Thus, IIQ wo=
uld create the employee account with CX UG and DWH admin users would use th=
e UI to add the DWH resources.&nbsp;</span></li>
         </ul></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <th scope=3D"row" class=3D"confluenceTh">DWH user resource assignme=
nts</th>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"e4d88b04-bad8-4a6e-8c20-128e89fd51d7">The DWH re=
sources are grouped separately (under resource type, "dwh_ui_module"), can =
be filtered for DWH use.</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"c5eb94e4-97c3-45cf-ae10-065933d5fc42">However, t=
hese resources are not bundled in any CX user packages; hence, a user updat=
e action in Compass will wipe all pre-assigned DWH resources without a mech=
anism to post them back.</li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">:cross:<span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">&n=
bsp;</span></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>See the use cases below.</p>
         <p>However, there is a NDS ticket to enhance the<em> list user res=
ource call</em> to filter by the DWH resource type only, preventing loading=
 the CX resources assigned to employee accounts.</p></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <th rowspan=3D"3" scope=3D"rowgroup" class=3D"confluenceTh">Manage =
DWH user tool</th>
        <th scope=3D"row" class=3D"confluenceTh">COR firm context</th>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"014a1cf8-c0ba-4190-8ebf-0e3d57143f79">The curren=
t tool works in the COR firm context only,=20
           <ul>
            <li data-uuid=3D"cb2db3ca-83ce-4833-8dc4-1ef60b912a56">The tool=
 is only access provisioned to COR firm users with the manage DWH user admi=
n right; and</li>
            <li data-uuid=3D"72576b23-7c22-4440-92eb-2bd060657028">All <em>=
shortId</em> accounts reside in the COR firm context.</li>
           </ul></li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"434311b4-be60-4b35-ab55-1055f3b9626d"><u>Conflic=
t:</u> However, Compass primary employee accounts can be set up in NBIN int=
ernal firm context or COR firm context.</li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">:tick:<span style=3D"color:#172b4d;"><sp=
an>&nbsp;</span></span></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>The DWH user mgmt tool must:</p>
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"d8ad30b5-1e3f-44f0-9d2e-55c76d84e90f">Be availab=
le to current DWH admin users, Darwin and Jenny, no matter which firm conte=
xt their primary accounts will be set up under during the Compass employee =
access launch; and&nbsp;</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"0f155490-32f2-4e03-af7b-c7f540fd0cf8">Allow DWH =
admin users to access all employee accounts, whether the accounts are in&nb=
sp; NBIN internal firm context and COR firm context; and</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"cf78fbd2-831b-4a33-9c8a-055669edf697">Continue t=
o support current employee accounts which are only assigned to DWH app acce=
ss, not CX access.</li>
         </ul></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <th scope=3D"row" class=3D"confluenceTh">List page</th>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"0fe5aca6-2730-4b95-a722-d830a6c0631b">These data=
 columns may become irrelevant or redundant:=20
           <ul>
            <li data-uuid=3D"d5579368-6f00-4990-a2e8-10c3c3c1ca56">User Gro=
up</li>
            <li data-uuid=3D"510732d5-9ca0-42db-9c4f-08261096e611">IDP User=
id</li>
            <li data-uuid=3D"4291a52a-676d-477a-a1d5-8525b4fba1ae">IDP Subj=
ect</li>
           </ul></li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">:cross:</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>No functional impact.</p>
         <p>Regression test: Must not break the UI if any data has become u=
navailable.</p></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <th scope=3D"row" class=3D"confluenceTh">Details modal</th>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Based on the discovery in the schema impacts above,</p>
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"bc802338-0586-4e48-a5d8-8f3a302eb5da"><strong>DW=
H user-to-UG relation</strong> must not be set to an employee's <em>shortId=
 </em>account in Compass</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"74d3ec39-7242-4379-8001-8078cdaae4b6">Likewise, =
the <strong>IDP user id</strong> must not be set either.</li>
         </ul>
         <p>:warning: <span>The IDP UserId is supposed to be populated by I=
IQ during auto-provisioning.&nbsp;</span></p></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">:tick:<span style=3D"color:#172b4d;"><sp=
an>&nbsp;</span></span></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">The DWH user mgmt tool m=
ust:</span></p>
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"0ab24fb1-56a9-472e-96df-c29646749cba">Disable th=
e capability of UG assignment; and</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"357b1705-0a17-4fe5-aab6-196aa4aca58e">Make the I=
DP UserId field read-only.</li>
         </ul>
         <p>Jira reference: <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://jira=
.bnc.ca/browse/NWPI-14671" rel=3D"nofollow">NWPI-14671<br></a></p></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <th scope=3D"row" class=3D"confluenceTh">Operational impact</th>
        <th scope=3D"row" class=3D"confluenceTh">Access request workflow</t=
h>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"fe6a10a6-520f-46aa-adb9-c7912c33d856">As the ass=
umption states, an employee must have Compass access before requesting Data=
 Solutions webapp access; therefore, the <em style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px=
;">shortId </em><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">account always exist=
s in Compass when the DWH admin users want to assign DWH resources to the e=
mployee; no "create user" scenario.&nbsp;</span></li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">:cross:</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p><span>For <strong>new employees,</strong> DWH admin users will =
be able to find the shortId account in CX and add the DWH resources to it.&=
nbsp;</span></p>
         <p><span>For<strong> job role/department change,</strong></span></=
p>
         <ul>
          <li><span>If the dept manager submits both CX access request AND =
DWH app access request to align the employee's access in the new role, ther=
e is no concern.</span></li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"6a872c53-5b1c-426a-be39-ac2d85f5c54b"><span>If t=
he dept manager only submits a CX access request, then the DWH user resourc=
e assignments for the employees will be wiped, and there will be a break in=
 the employee's webapp access. It shall be handled as a support case via BA=
U process.</span></li>
         </ul>
         <p>:warning: Attention: For DWH admin user</p></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <th scope=3D"row" class=3D"confluenceTh">Access monitoring</th>
        <th scope=3D"row" class=3D"confluenceTh">User certification</th>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"f0d2854e-a385-4dd5-9325-d3723b970946">Data Solut=
ions webapps are operated under different application ids, and governed by =
IIQ user certification independently.</li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">:cross:</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p><span>No requirement on producing any report on the correlation=
 between CX access and DWH access from Compass db.</span></p></td>
       </tr>
      </tbody>
     </table>
    </div>
    <p><br></p>
